# AI Smell — verify before you claim done

AI output often looks right before it is right. Before reporting success, run these checks on your own work:

## Smell → check

| Smell | Quick check |
|-------|-------------|
| **Fabricated references** | Grep/docs: do functions, APIs, flags, endpoints actually exist? |
| **Cargo-cult patterns** | Does this pattern solve a problem here, or just look familiar? |
| **Shallow error handling** | Does each catch block name a specific failure and recovery? |
| **Mirror tests** | Do tests assert requirements, not just re-implement the code? |
| **Symmetry without substance** | Would swapping bullets/items change the meaning? If not, cut filler |

## Struggle signal

If you fail repeatedly in one module, stop guessing — report that the area may need refactor (hidden state, tangled deps) and ask how to proceed.

## On uncertainty

Flag inferred values as unverified. Do not present guesses as facts.
